## Memory Architecture
This system uses 4 layers:
1. This file (MEMORY.md) — durable operating knowledge, always loaded
2. ~/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md — daily notes, written by nightly cron; read for recent context
3. ~/life/ — PARA knowledge graph (Projects, Areas, Resources, Archives); read summary.md files for fast entity context, items.json for atomic facts
4. ~/sessions/ — rich conversation logs (research, decisions, brainstorms)

Auto-recall (UserPromptSubmit hook):
- Fires on every message before the agent responds
- Extracts key terms from the prompt, searches across all 4 layers
- Script: ~/.agent/scripts/auto-recall.py
- Hook wrapper: ~/.agent/scripts/hooks/auto-recall.sh
- Output injected as system context — the agent sees relevant memories automatically

When to write:
- MEMORY.md: only for preferences, rules, and patterns that should persist forever
- ~/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md: nightly cron handles this; the agent can also append during session
- ~/life/: when learning durable facts about a project, person, or area
- ~/sessions/: after any significant conversation worth revisiting

## Background Workers
Long-running tasks run as background headless sessions.
- Spawn: run ~/.agent/scripts/spawn-worker.sh "description" "prompt" /workdir
- Check status: ls ~/.agent/workers/active/
- Heartbeat runs every 15 min and reports completions to Slack
- Workers write [STATUS: ...] and [DONE: ...] markers to their logs

## Self-Improving Feedback System
- Auto-feedback capture: feedback-detector.py runs on every UserPromptSubmit, detects correction patterns, queues to ~/.agent/feedback-queue.jsonl
- Review pending feedback: python3 ~/.agent/scripts/process-feedback.py
- Corrections become persistent memories so the same mistake isn't repeated

## Key Paths
- Knowledge graph: ~/life/
- Daily notes: ~/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md
- Session notes: ~/sessions/
- Worker scripts: ~/.agent/scripts/
- Active workers: ~/.agent/workers/active/
- Cron jobs: ~/.agent/cron/jobs.json
- Logs: ~/.agent/logs/

